  "body": "The Bank of Kestria has completed a recovery exercise for the system that settles large payments between regulated banks. During the exercise on 27 September, staff transferred test operations from Saltmarsh to the Bank's backup site in Amberford. The exercise used simulated payment instructions and did not move customer funds.\n\nAll 14 participating institutions connected successfully to the backup service. Processing resumed after 43 minutes, within the Bank's internal recovery limit of 60 minutes. The test included the loss of a primary communications link and a check that completed instructions could not be processed twice.\n\nObservers identified two areas for improvement: clearer contact arrangements during staff changes and faster confirmation that every participant had received the recovery message. Neither affected the completion of the exercise. The Bank has assigned corrective actions and will track them through its operational risk programme. Normal settlement services remained available throughout."
